# Lumina OpenClaw Community Code of Conduct

Lumina OpenClaw welcomes contributors with different backgrounds, identities,
experience levels, languages, and points of view. We want participation in this
project to be constructive, safe, and focused on building useful software.

## Expected behavior

- Be respectful, patient, and specific when giving feedback.
- Discuss ideas and code without attacking the person who proposed them.
- Welcome questions and help new contributors understand the project.
- Respect privacy, attribution, licenses, and the boundaries of other people.
- Accept maintainer decisions gracefully, even when a proposal is not merged.
- Disclose conflicts of interest and meaningful AI assistance when relevant.

## Unacceptable behavior

- Harassment, discrimination, threats, stalking, or personal attacks.
- Sexualized language or unwanted attention.
- Publishing another person's private information without permission.
- Spam, deliberate disruption, impersonation, or deceptive contributions.
- Sharing credentials, private conversations, personal data, or harmful code.
- Repeatedly ignoring reasonable maintainer or moderation instructions.

## Scope

This code applies to repository issues, pull requests, reviews, discussions,
project documentation, and other public spaces where someone represents Lumina
OpenClaw.

## Reporting and enforcement

For an immediate public problem, flag the content using GitHub's reporting tools
and avoid escalating the exchange. For a private report, contact repository
owner **DAL NIJARUQ** through the contact method listed on the
[@I24D GitHub profile](https://github.com/I24D). Do not post sensitive evidence
in a public issue.

The maintainer may edit or remove content, lock conversations, reject
contributions, or temporarily or permanently restrict participation. Decisions
will consider context, impact, prior behavior, and the safety of the community.
